I think something like this should work:

Output the following files:

- `dist/cjs/mermaid.js`
- `dist/cjs/mermaid.min.js`
- `dist/cjs/package.json` indicates `.js` / `.ts` files in this directory are CJS
  ```jsonc
  {
    "type": "commonjs"
  }
  ```
- `dist/cjs/mermaid.d.ts`
  ```ts
  declare const mermaid: typeof import('../mermaid.js').default
  export as namespace mermaid
  export = mermaid
  ```
- `package.json`:
  ```jsonc
  {
    "types": "./dist/mermaid.d.ts",
    "exports": {
      ".": {
        // The `types` export is not necessary if the `.d.ts` filename matches the `.js` one.
        "require": "./dist/cjs/mermaid.d.ts",
        // "import" should be redundant. "default" is sufficient if "type": "module" is set.
        "default": {
          // The types export is needed, because the `dist/mermaid.d.ts` filename doesn’t match the `dist/mermaid.core.mjs` base name and extension.
          "types": "./dist/mermaid.d.ts",
          "default": "./dist/mermaid.core.mjs",
        }
      }
    }
  }
  ```
